--- WHAT SHIPPED (6 files, established per-surface multi-file pattern) ---------------
  SectionErrorBoundary.Model.swift    (297 ln) P1/S11 telemetry seam (view.opened +
        boundary.caught — the latter a port of the web ErrorBoundary.componentDidCatch
        [ErrorBoundary:name] structured log), the input snapshot (hasError / errorMessage /
        resetKey), the resolved view-state + Phase (healthy | caught(message)), the pure
        SectionErrorBoundaryProjection (web `hasError ? fallback : children` + whitespace
        message trim), the P1/S8 SectionErrorBoundarySource seam + InMemory source, the
        @Observable @MainActor model (resetKey-change clear = web getDerivedStateFromProps;
        retry clear+count = web handleRetry; once-only view.opened), a pure a11y label
        adapter, and the P1/S10 strings facade. No SwiftUI / no networking.
  SectionErrorBoundary.swift          (118 ln) main View. Generic over wrapped Content +
        optional custom Fallback. Three variant initializers mirror the web precedence
        (fallback > fallbackTitle > inline). onAppear→start / onDisappear→stop.
        surfaceSlug = "SectionErrorBoundary".
  SectionErrorBoundary.Views.swift    (158 ln) the inline fallback (web ErrorBoundary inline
        — alert chrome + "Component failed to load" + truncated message + working Retry) and
        the titled fallback (web fallbackTitle — alert chrome + title + the reassurance
        subtitle), plus the shared danger-tinted alert chrome (web rounded-xl border-tesla-
        red/20 bg-tesla-red/5 p-4 → statusDanger tokens). role="alert" → combined VoiceOver
        element; the Retry button stays a separate focusable/actionable element.
  SectionErrorBoundary.Previews.swift (87 ln)  healthy / inline-error / titled-error /
        custom-fallback previews (DEBUG).
  SectionErrorBoundary.strings        (23 ln)  table "SectionErrorBoundary": the web source
        key errors.section.subtitle + the inline fallback copy the wrapped web ErrorBoundary
        hardcodes (errors.section.componentFailed, errors.section.retry). No English literals
        remain in the Swift sources.
  SectionErrorBoundary.Tests.swift    (209 ln) 3 suites / 14 tests (projection / model+
        telemetry+reset+retry / a11y).

  States reproduced (faithful to the web source — an error boundary, NOT a data-fetch leaf,
  so it has no loading/empty/stale/offline lifecycle; reproducing those would be invented
  drift). Every branch of the web source renders:
    • healthy        → the wrapped content renders.
    • caught/inline  → default fallback: alert chrome + "Component failed to load" + the
                       captured message + a working Retry (web `ErrorBoundary inline`).
    • caught/titled  → `fallbackTitle` set: alert chrome + title + subtitle
                       "Other parts of the page should still work." (no Retry).
    • caught/custom  → `fallback` node set: the caller's view renders (no Retry).
  Plus the wrapped boundary's resetKey-change clear + handleRetry, ported in the model.

